<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
  <title>Privacy notice — <%= p.name %></title>
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex">
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#ffffff">
  <link rel="icon" href="/img/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter+Tight:wght@600;700;800&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css">
</head>
<body>
  <header class="nav">
    <div class="wrap">
      <a href="/" class="nav__brand"><%= p.name %></a>
      <nav class="nav__links" aria-label="Primary"><a href="/#about">About</a><a href="/#services">What I do</a><a href="/#events">Events</a><a href="/#contact">Contact</a></nav>
      <button class="nav__burger" type="button" aria-label="Open menu" aria-expanded="false"><span></span><span></span></button>
    </div>
  </header>
  <main class="prose">
    <span class="kicker">Privacy notice</span>
    <h1>What this site records about visitors</h1>
    <p>umitbozdag.com is the personal website of <%= p.name %>, London. Like most websites it keeps a visitor log. When you open a page, the server records:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Your IP address</strong> — the network address your visit comes from.</li>
      <li><strong>Your browser and device type</strong> — taken from the browser’s user-agent string (for example “Chrome on Windows, desktop”) — and your browser language.</li>
      <li><strong>Your approximate location</strong> — the country and city associated with your IP address, as reported by the hosting platform or by the geolocation service ipapi.co. This is never more precise than city level.</li>
      <li>The page you opened, the site that referred you (if any) and the time of the visit.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>No cookies are set for visitors and no tracking or advertising scripts are loaded. The site does not use analytics providers; the log stays on the server that hosts it.</p>
    <h2>Why</h2>
    <p>To understand who visits the site — for example which countries and cities interest in my work comes from — and to keep the site secure. The legal basis is legitimate interest. The records are not used for advertising, profiling or marketing, and they are not sold or passed to third parties.</p>
    <h2>Where it is kept and for how long</h2>
    <p>Records are stored on the server that hosts this website and in its hosting provider’s logs, and are kept for up to 12 months before being deleted. Only <%= p.name %> has access to them.</p>
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>You can ask to see or delete any record relating to you at any time by emailing <a href="mailto:<%= p.email %>"><%= p.email %></a>. If you would rather your real IP address was not recorded, browse through a VPN.</p>
    <h2>Contact form and WhatsApp</h2>
    <p>Messages sent through the contact form are delivered to <%= p.name %> by email and used only to reply to you. The WhatsApp button opens a chat with <%= p.firstName %> in WhatsApp; WhatsApp’s own privacy policy then applies.</p>
    <p><a href="/">← Back to the site</a></p>
  </main>
  <footer class="footer">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span>© <%= year %> <%= p.name %> · Web design by <%= p.name %> — all rights reserved.</span>
      <nav aria-label="Footer"><a href="/">umitbozdag.com →</a></nav>
    </div>
  </footer>
  <script src="/js/main.js" defer></script>
</body>
</html>
